---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import EyeIcon from '../components/EyeIcon.astro';
import RegistryDialog from '../components/RegistryDialog.astro';
import {data, href} from '../lib/data';
const eyes = data('end-eyes', []);
const bosses = data('bosses', []);
---
<Layout title="Bosses & the End" description="Find every End Remastered eye, prepare the required offerings and explore the boss encounters of Towns & Kingdoms.">
 <p class="eyebrow">Handbook / Adventure</p>
 <h1>Bosses & the End</h1>
 <p class="intro">Sixteen boss encounters each award a different End Remastered eye. Collect any twelve to open the End portal.</p>
 <nav class="toc-inline" aria-label="Boss guide sections"><a href="#end-portal">Opening the portal</a><a href="#eye-routes">Boss eye drops</a><a href="#eye-guide">Encounter preparation</a><a href="#encounters">All encounters</a></nav>

 <section id="end-portal" class="section prose">
  <p class="eyebrow">End Remastered / The journey</p><h2>Twelve different eyes</h2>
  <ol class="portal-steps">
   <li><strong>Collect twelve distinct eye types.</strong> Use the table below to find the boss that drops each eye.</li>
   <li><strong>Locate a Stronghold.</strong> You can still throw ordinary Eyes of Ender to find it. Custom eyes also point the way, with a 10% chance to break when thrown; keep your rare finds for the portal.</li>
   <li><strong>Fill all twelve frames with different custom eyes.</strong> Stronghold frames begin empty. A duplicate eye type is rejected, and an ordinary Eye of Ender cannot fill a frame.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="callout"><strong>Choose your encounters</strong><p>Pick the bosses you want to fight. Some encounters require an offering or have their own entry requirements. You can explore other dimensions and summon the Wither before completing the End portal.</p></div>
 </section>

 <section id="eye-routes" class="section">
  <h2>Boss eye drops</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table class="eye-table"><thead><tr><th>Eye</th><th>Boss</th><th>Dimension</th></tr></thead><tbody>{eyes.map((eye:any)=><tr><td><a class="eye-name" href={'#eye-'+eye.id.split(':')[1]}><EyeIcon eye={eye} size={26} />{eye.name}</a></td><td><button class="table-button" data-detail={eye.bossId}>{eye.bossName}</button></td><td class="table-detail">{eye.dimension}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
 </section>

 <section id="eye-guide" class="section">
  <p class="eyebrow">Field guide / Locations & offerings</p><h2>Prepare each expedition</h2>
  <p>Appraise your equipment, allocate your skill points and bring food and recovery supplies before activating an encounter. The level shown is the enemy’s configured floor, not a required player level. Bosses can scale above that floor with nearby players.</p>
  <div class="eye-grid">{eyes.map((eye:any)=><article class="card eye-card" id={'eye-'+eye.id.split(':')[1]}>
   <header class="eye-heading"><EyeIcon eye={eye} size={40} /><div><h3>{eye.name}</h3><code>{eye.id}</code></div></header>
   <div class="tags"><span class="tag">{eye.dimension}</span>{eye.minimumLevel!==null&&<span class="tag tag-gold">Enemy L{eye.minimumLevel}+ · {eye.classification}</span>}</div>
   <h4><button class="table-button" data-detail={eye.bossId}>{eye.bossName}</button></h4>
   <dl class="eye-facts"><div><dt>Find it</dt><dd>{eye.location}</dd></div><div><dt>Begin the encounter</dt><dd>{eye.activation}</dd></div><div><dt>Prepare</dt><dd>{eye.preparation}</dd></div></dl>
   {eye.notableRewards.length>0&&<div class="eye-rewards"><h4>Notable rewards</h4><p>{eye.notableRewards.map((reward:any,index:number)=><>{index>0?' · ':''}{reward.name}</>)}</p></div>}
   {eye.rewardPool.length>0&&<p class="eye-pool"><button class="table-button" data-detail={eye.bossId}>View the equipment reward pool →</button></p>}
  </article>)}</div>
 </section>

 <section id="encounters" class="section">
  <p class="eyebrow">Reference / {bosses.length} encounters</p><h2>Encounter registry</h2>
  <p>Browse bosses and elite enemies across the pack. Reward pools list possible equipment selections; their entries are alternatives rather than a promise that every item drops together. Appraisal reveals sealed equipment.</p>
  <div class="encounter-notes"><div class="callout"><strong>Enemy levels</strong><p>Ordinary bosses use the higher of their floor or the nearby player’s level +10, up to level 110. Configured elite encounters cap at 100. These values describe enemy scaling, not entry locks.</p></div><div class="callout"><strong>Equipment rewards</strong><p>Dedicated equipment pools require a player kill. A boss’s equipment reward tier is separate from its combat level and weapon handling style. <a href={href('loot/')}>Read about appraisal and rarity →</a></p></div></div>
  <div data-registry="bosses"><div class="toolbar"><input type="search" data-filter="query" placeholder="Search an encounter or mod…" aria-label="Search bosses"/><select data-filter="modName" aria-label="Filter by mod"><option value="">All mods</option></select><select data-filter="classification" aria-label="Filter encounter type"><option value="">All encounters</option></select></div><div class="results-meta"><span data-count>Finding encounters…</span><span>Select an encounter for its rewards</span></div><div class="weapon-grid" data-results></div><div class="pagination"><button data-prev disabled>← Previous</button><span data-page-label>1 / 1</span><button data-next>Next →</button></div></div>
 </section>
 <RegistryDialog />
 <script>import '../scripts/registry';</script>
</Layout>
<style>
 .portal-steps{padding-left:24px}.portal-steps li{padding-left:5px;margin:15px 0;line-height:1.8}
 .eye-table td{vertical-align:top}.eye-name{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap}
 .eye-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:18px;margin-top:26px}.eye-card{padding:26px;scroll-margin-top:95px}.eye-heading{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;margin-bottom:18px}.eye-heading h3{margin:0 0 5px;font-size:21px}.eye-heading>div{min-width:0}.eye-heading code{overflow-wrap:anywhere;font-size:13px;color:var(--muted)}.eye-card>.tags{margin-bottom:22px}.eye-card h4{font-size:14px;margin:20px 0 9px}.eye-card h4>.table-button{font-size:15px;font-weight:650;text-align:left}.eye-facts{margin:0}.eye-facts>div{margin-top:15px}.eye-facts dt{font-size:13px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.11em;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:5px}.eye-facts dd{margin:0;font-size:16px;line-height:1.8;color:var(--muted)}.eye-rewards p{font-size:16px;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:0}.eye-pool{margin:8px 0 0!important}.eye-pool button{font-size:14px}.encounter-notes{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:18px;margin:24px 0}.encounter-notes .callout{margin:0}.encounter-notes p{font-size:16px;margin-bottom:0}
 @media(max-width:760px){.eye-grid,.encounter-notes{grid-template-columns:1fr}.eye-card{padding:22px}.eye-table th,.eye-table td{padding:14px 12px}.eye-name{white-space:normal}}
</style>
